1
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:49,020
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:51,990
[Episode 27]

3
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,509
Shen Fuxuan is
the only one absent today, right?

4
00:01:56,509 --> 00:01:57,920
He has a shift at the hospital.

5
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:58,979
He told me about it.

6
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,070
Listen to this.

7
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,120
It's good to be busy. Let him be.

8
00:02:03,430 --> 00:02:04,230
Listen.

9
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,710
Sorry, guys.

10
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,870
I'm on duty today
and really can't make it.

11
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:08,930
I'll treat you guys

12
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:09,710
next time.

13
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,010
All right, Shen.

14
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,000
It's a deal!

15
00:02:13,190 --> 00:02:14,000
That's it.

16
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,960
It's a voice message,

17
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,000
not a phone call.

18
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:20,840
When I saw the message today,

19
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,590
saying Zeqiu was going to treat us
to a meal—

20
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:23,190
I'm not exaggerating—

21
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:24,520
I really read it 3 times.

22
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:26,750
Zeqiu would treat us to a meal?

23
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:28,810
I felt the same way.

24
00:02:29,630 --> 00:02:30,910
Have I never treated you guys before?

25
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:32,400
Nope.

26
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:34,280
Exactly!

27
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,190
Zeqiu,

28
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,800
why on earth are you treating us

29
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,000
to this meal?

30
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,120
If you don't tell us, we dare not eat.

31
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,090
You ungrateful people
really broke my heart.

32
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:45,680
Don't talk about my brother like that.

33
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,680
My brother is just somewhat frugal.

34
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,560
We should encourage this behavior.

35
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:52,360
Then maybe he'll finally
spend more in the future.

36
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,090
So you are the biggest ingrate.

37
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,200
Alright, let's get to the point.

38
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,870
There is indeed some serious news

39
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:01,670
I'd like to share with everyone.

40
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,680
Our Dr. Lin Zhixia's

41
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:07,030
application for a national key
scientific research project

42
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:07,590
got approved.

43
00:03:07,590 --> 00:03:08,720
A round of applause!

44
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:12,560
Congratulations
on achieving one more goal.

45
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,560
Zhixia, you really make me proud.

46
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:15,870
It's a national project!

47
00:03:15,870 --> 00:03:18,070
I have something else to brag about now.

48
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,430
I also helped with this, right?

49
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:21,840
Shut up. Nobody asked.

50
00:03:22,630 --> 00:03:24,360
Tell Mom and Dad about this later.

51
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,030
They will be happy for you, too.

52
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:26,630
Yeah.

53
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:28,680
Lin Zhixia has prepared
for this project for so long.

54
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,840
Her efforts have finally paid off.

55
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,360
Come on, I propose a toast

56
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,280
to her achievement!

57
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,240
-Absolutely, cheers.
-Cheers.

58
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:33,960
Hold on.

59
00:03:34,079 --> 00:03:34,960
Jiang Yubai,

60
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,680
Zeqiu is celebrating for his sister.

61
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:40,520
So in what capacity are you

62
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,910
proposing this toast?

63
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,150
I...

64
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,960
As the doctor's family, of course.

65
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:50,120
Jiang, you have to drink this up.

66
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:50,870
I'll drink it up.

67
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:52,120
-Come on.
-Cheers!

68
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:53,150
Cheers.

69
00:03:58,870 --> 00:04:01,030
That was a toast to Lin Zhixia.

70
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,020
I have one more thing to announce.

71
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,960
Well...

72
00:04:06,150 --> 00:04:07,240
Jin Baihui and I

73
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:11,350
are getting married.

74
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,280
G-Getting married?

75
00:04:15,430 --> 00:04:16,310
Getting married.

76
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,240
This is big news!

77
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,720
Am I the only one who didn't know?

78
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,800
No, I really didn't know this.

79
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,529
I hadn't heard a thing about it.

80
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:23,920
I only knew a tiny part of it.

81
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,630
I knew even less than a tiny part.

82
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:29,360
What...

83
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,920
Good for you, Zeqiu.

84
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:33,360
You've been working on
something so big secretly.

85
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:33,950
Baihui,

86
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:35,360
are we going to change how we address you

87
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,480
and call you "sister-in-law"?

88
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:39,159
Let's hear it.

89
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:42,090
Getting me to change
how I address you is not easy.

90
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,120
You don't need to change.

91
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,830
I don't mean to be a wet blanket,

92
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:49,430
but what about your parents?

93
00:04:52,870 --> 00:04:54,360
We've already made up our minds.

94
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,430
We will be together

95
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,050
no matter what they say.

96
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:03,560
Hold on.

97
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,240
I knew

98
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:07,510
there must be

99
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:11,090
something fishy
about this rare meal you treated us to.

100
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:12,750
Lin Zhixia,

101
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:14,510
Lin Zeqiu,

102
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:17,240
you two want to use this one meal

103
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,630
to celebrate two happy events?

104
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,000
Is that appropriate?

105
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,720
Yeah, it shouldn't be this simple.

106
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:24,120
You should at least
treat us to another meal, right?

107
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:24,870
At least two.

108
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:26,600
Fine, fine, as many meals as you want.

109
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:28,000
Let's see if they can
stop you from whining.

110
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,360
Since the "sister-in-law" said so,

111
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:30,240
let's have a toast.

112
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,830
-Come on. Cheers.
-Cheers.

113
00:05:31,950 --> 00:05:33,870
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

114
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:39,270
Can we start eating now?

115
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:40,270
Eat up.

116
00:05:40,270 --> 00:05:40,920
There's nothing else, huh?

117
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,680
No.

118
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:55,310
I was really happy
having dinner with everyone today.

119
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:57,310
Since you're home,

120
00:05:57,310 --> 00:05:59,920
I'm heading back now.

121
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:01,180
How about you stay?

122
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:04,950
Okay.

123
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,410
You're going to sleep on the floor?

124
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:22,000
Yep, I'll sleep here.

125
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:25,240
Aren't you my boyfriend?

126
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:26,740
We can sleep together.

127
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:02,070
I'm so happy today.

128
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,950
Your heart is racing.

129
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,050
What's on your mind?

130
00:07:18,630 --> 00:07:19,680
I'm wondering

131
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,680
if I can kiss you.

132
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,910
♪ Warm fishbowl ♪

133
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,540
♪ Glass sprouts forth ♪

134
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,610
♪ Drowning at dusk ♪

135
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,180
♪ You come to save me ♪

136
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,410
♪ Such oddities ♪

137
00:08:18,450 --> 00:08:20,250
♪ Bizarre dreams ♪

138
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:22,470
♪ You call them ♪

139
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:25,050
♪ Déjà vu ♪

140
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,940
♪ A random cut-in ♪

141
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:29,790
♪ 2013 ♪

142
00:08:30,230 --> 00:08:31,990
♪ 16 times faster ♪

143
00:08:32,909 --> 00:08:34,870
♪ The night is like a window ♪

144
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,440
Why did you turn off the light?

145
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,240
To sleep.

146
00:08:40,789 --> 00:08:42,520
Do you sleep with the lights on?

147
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:48,360
By sleeping, you mean...

148
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,480
Dad, you're here.

149
00:09:35,790 --> 00:09:36,720
Mr. and Mrs. Jin.

150
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,930
What's this all about?

151
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:40,510
Please sit down first.

152
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:42,600
Mom, have a seat.

153
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:49,600
Well...

154
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,080
Mr. and Mrs. Jin,

155
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:52,270
today...

156
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:53,330
You sit down first.

157
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,910
I'd like to discuss with you
the relationship

158
00:09:57,910 --> 00:09:59,370
between Jin Baihui and me.

159
00:10:00,390 --> 00:10:02,590
We don't approve of your relationship.

160
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,000
You called and asked us to have a talk.

161
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,660
I thought you had come around.

162
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,610
Mom, actually, I...

163
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,790
Lin Zeqiu and I...

164
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:13,510
Lin,

165
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,450
let's make things clear today.

166
00:10:17,670 --> 00:10:21,270
Our family doesn't approve
of you and Jin Baihui being together,

167
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:24,010
because I don't think
you two are a good match.

168
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:26,000
Given your family background,

169
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,120
your job,

170
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,450
and your financial situation,

171
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,980
you're not suitable for her in every way.

172
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:38,280
Jin Baihui should find someone
with a better background.

173
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,390
Of course,

174
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,840
you could also find someone
with a better background.

175
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,240
This way, you'll face much less stress

176
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,440
in life in the future.

177
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:49,170
We are doing this for your own good.

178
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,080
At your age,

179
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:53,600
you think marriage is all about love.

180
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:54,720
We got it,

181
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,440
because we were also once your age.

182
00:10:59,150 --> 00:11:00,750
But at our age,

183
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,940
we know the truth about marriage.

184
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:05,120
This is the last chance

185
00:11:05,550 --> 00:11:06,600
for you to change

186
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,840
the course of your lives.

187
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,550
This is a big deal,

188
00:11:11,550 --> 00:11:12,630
not a joke.

189
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:15,610
Since we are on this topic,

190
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:18,330
we don't want to make things too awkward.

191
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,600
You two should break up peacefully.

192
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:24,770
Mr. and Mrs. Jin,

193
00:11:24,870 --> 00:11:25,750
I understand what you mean.

194
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:27,010
How about we eat first?

195
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:27,960
Baihui specifically ordered

196
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,220
your favorite dishes.

197
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:33,230
-Let's talk over dinner.
-Actually, today...

198
00:11:35,910 --> 00:11:37,910
I'm here to inform you of something.

199
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:40,750
Lin Zeqiu and I have

200
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,120
already registered our marriage.

201
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:44,910
What?

202
00:11:47,630 --> 00:11:49,760
These are our marriage certificates.

203
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,530
Mr. and Mrs. Jin,

204
00:11:53,870 --> 00:11:56,080
although this decision
was made a bit hastily,

205
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,790
we have thought it through.

206
00:11:57,810 --> 00:11:59,320
Jin Baihui, are you crazy?

207
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:01,840
Mrs. Jin, this is mostly...

208
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:02,360
Shut up!

209
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:05,550
Jin Baihui,

210
00:12:05,870 --> 00:12:07,600
are you going to drive me crazy?

211
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,820
Mr. Jin, it's all my fault.

212
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:10,840
This is on me.

213
00:12:13,030 --> 00:12:14,090
Let me talk to them.

214
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:30,090
This is not because you are dissatisfied
with Lin Zeqiu,

215
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,320
nor is it because I didn't find

216
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,720
a better person to marry.

217
00:12:35,870 --> 00:12:37,120
It's because I didn't listen
to your arrangements,

218
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,510
and I got out of your control.

219
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:40,040
That's why you are unhappy.

220
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:47,510
Dad,

221
00:12:48,550 --> 00:12:49,120
Mom,

222
00:12:52,790 --> 00:12:53,870
how long has it been

223
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,200
since we had a proper talk last time?

224
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,440
You only criticize me,

225
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,600
lecture me, and show disappointment in me.

226
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,440
It feels like nothing I do
is ever good enough.

227
00:13:12,510 --> 00:13:14,440
But is this how we should get along?

228
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:22,750
Dad, do you remember?

229
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,510
When I was little, and you took me to sing

230
00:13:26,510 --> 00:13:27,970
in the Children's Palace,

231
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,870
you told me,

232
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:32,530
"Baihui, you should sing loudly,

233
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,750
so I can hear your voice."

234
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:38,120
So I sang with all my strength.

235
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,290
No other kid could drown out my voice.

236
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:42,020
Even the teacher laughed at me.

237
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,030
Because that way,

238
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:45,360
you could stand outside

239
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,600
and hear your daughter sing.

240
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,870
I finally stepped onto the stage

241
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:53,200
at the school anniversary gala that year.

242
00:13:53,630 --> 00:13:55,090
I know you wouldn't agree,

243
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:56,550
so I practiced

244
00:13:56,550 --> 00:13:57,670
and performed in secret.

245
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,930
I felt so happy to be rebellious for once.

246
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,360
But I kept staring at the audience,

247
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:08,440
not because

248
00:14:09,670 --> 00:14:11,670
the students' cheers made me proud.

249
00:14:13,510 --> 00:14:16,170
I was actually trying to find you two
down there.

250
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,250
I was wondering.

251
00:14:21,150 --> 00:14:22,790
If you saw me on stage,

252
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,910
if you heard my voice,

253
00:14:27,150 --> 00:14:29,610
would you be
a little more satisfied with me?

254
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:34,120
Would you be happier?

255
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:47,000
Mom,

256
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,810
after I started school,

257
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,410
getting me into Qingbei University

258
00:14:52,410 --> 00:14:54,080
was your everything.

259
00:14:56,550 --> 00:14:58,010
You stayed up late with me,

260
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:00,970
accompanied me to exams,
and studied with me.

261
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,000
But how long has it been

262
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
since you went on a proper vacation?

263
00:15:05,870 --> 00:15:09,070
How long has it been
since you truly lived for yourselves?

264
00:15:12,270 --> 00:15:13,120
I know

265
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,810
how many cigarettes you smoked

266
00:15:16,550 --> 00:15:19,750
on the balcony, Dad,
when I had to repeat a grade that year.

267
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,960
And Mom, I saw you crying secretly

268
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,240
in the kitchen.

269
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:29,240
I've been listening to you all these years

270
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:29,960
because...

271
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,750
It's not because I didn't dare to rebel.

272
00:15:32,750 --> 00:15:34,200
It's because I couldn't bear to rebel.

273
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:36,670
I couldn't bear to see you hurt again.

274
00:15:51,630 --> 00:15:53,240
Actually, I feel that I'm quite a failure

275
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,240
as a daughter.

276
00:15:59,550 --> 00:16:00,630
How did I

277
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,600
lose the parents
who once loved me so much?

278
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:12,910
Baihui.

279
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:22,510
Dad just wanted you to live

280
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,200
a happier life

281
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,200
and go further.

282
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,170
Mr. and Mrs. Jin,

283
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,720
I understand

284
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,550
your concerns.

285
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:48,930
There is no parent
who doesn't love their child.

286
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:51,400
Maybe one day in the future,

287
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,170
when we become parents,

288
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,650
we might make the same choice you've made.

289
00:16:58,270 --> 00:16:59,320
But today,

290
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:02,910
I hope you two

291
00:17:04,310 --> 00:17:05,750
can give us a chance

292
00:17:06,550 --> 00:17:07,810
and trust us this once.

293
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,069
I will do my best

294
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:14,240
in the rest of my life to prove

295
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,329
that I haven't betrayed your trust today,

296
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,240
and that Jin Baihui made the right choice.

297
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,160
Please

298
00:17:24,510 --> 00:17:25,550
give me a chance.

299
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:52,750
I'm thirsty.

300
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:57,020
Pour me a cup of tea.

301
00:17:59,270 --> 00:17:59,920
Mr. Jin.

302
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:11,580
Please have some tea, Mr. Jin.

303
00:18:18,830 --> 00:18:20,590
Mrs. Jin, please have some tea.

304
00:18:22,590 --> 00:18:24,350
I didn't prepare a gift for you.

305
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,510
No need, no need.

306
00:18:29,030 --> 00:18:29,960
Let's eat first.

307
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:48,150
[Watch out for the train]

308
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:49,180
You're finally back, man.

309
00:18:49,550 --> 00:18:51,240
I thought you weren't going to repay

310
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:52,500
this last bit of money.

311
00:18:52,790 --> 00:18:53,550
No way.

312
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,130
Give me a moment.

313
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:59,680
[Watch out for the train]

314
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:05,700
[Watch out for the train]

315
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:16,600
This is the last payment.

316
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:17,780
We are even now.

317
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,620
You're really something.

318
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:27,310
I never expected that

319
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:29,680
you could pull through all these years.

320
00:19:30,030 --> 00:19:32,690
Actually, you didn't
have to repay it back then.

321
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:34,750
But you still did it,

322
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:36,920
so your family and friends
wouldn't suffer losses.

323
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:37,920
You're a real man.

324
00:19:40,590 --> 00:19:41,680
Still, thank you

325
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,130
for lending me the money back then.

326
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,660
Contact me anytime if you need anything.

327
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,790
After all,
we've known each other for years.

328
00:19:48,790 --> 00:19:49,440
Thanks.

329
00:20:07,570 --> 00:20:09,300
[Contacts]

330
00:20:09,420 --> 00:20:10,830
[Peng][More]

331
00:20:10,860 --> 00:20:12,410
[Delete Contact]

332
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:14,560
[Delete this contact?]

333
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:15,950
[Contacts]

334
00:20:50,510 --> 00:20:51,160
Zhixia,

335
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:53,160
the project you're leading
has been included

336
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:55,020
in the national key support list.

337
00:20:55,270 --> 00:20:57,680
But next,
the project is going to be upgraded,

338
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:00,200
and we will face
more complex resource integration

339
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,530
and management issues.

340
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:05,200
Of course,
it will also receive greater support.

341
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,080
So the school has decided

342
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:10,590
to make Qianche lead the later work.

343
00:21:10,830 --> 00:21:13,760
You need to hand over the project
as soon as possible.

344
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:19,780
I got replaced?

345
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:23,830
But I have been in charge

346
00:21:23,830 --> 00:21:25,790
of this project from the very beginning.

347
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:28,030
I'm familiar
with all the data and materials.

348
00:21:28,030 --> 00:21:30,000
I've even had a plan for the next step.

349
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,460
How could you get me replaced
all of a sudden?

350
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:34,750
Professor,

351
00:21:35,510 --> 00:21:37,700
this project was planned
and pushed forward

352
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:38,830
by Lin Zhixia alone.

353
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,570
I think she is fully capable

354
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:42,510
of completing the follow-up work.

355
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:44,040
Even if there's an upgrade,

356
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:47,070
we don't need to change
the person in charge, do we?

357
00:21:47,510 --> 00:21:49,440
The operational difficulty
of a national project

358
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:52,170
has increased
by more than an order of magnitude.

359
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:54,070
With your current management experience,

360
00:21:54,070 --> 00:21:55,200
you can't handle it.

361
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,840
At this stage, it would be

362
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,730
better for Qianche to lead.

363
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:04,270
No, I still think it's better

364
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,960
for Lin Zhixia
to finish this project herself.

365
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,270
She knows this project best.

366
00:22:08,270 --> 00:22:08,920
Qianche,

367
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:11,200
there must be a reason

368
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,930
for the school's arrangement.

369
00:22:15,030 --> 00:22:16,290
Don't you understand?

370
00:22:26,550 --> 00:22:28,480
Then what will I be responsible for

371
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,810
after the handover?

372
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:33,920
The school and the country
have higher expectations for you.

373
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,680
As for your specific responsibilities,

374
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:36,310
well,

375
00:22:37,070 --> 00:22:38,870
I'll tell you separately later.

376
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:50,460
[Lin Zhixia]

377
00:22:54,560 --> 00:22:57,560
[Lin Zhixia]

378
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:01,040
Why are you still up so late?

379
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:03,000
I can't sleep.

380
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:04,810
I want to chat with you.

381
00:23:09,590 --> 00:23:10,390
What's wrong?

382
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:13,200
Did something happen at school?

383
00:23:14,070 --> 00:23:15,200
Ms. Wu asked me

384
00:23:16,590 --> 00:23:19,400
to hand the project over to Senior Tan.

385
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:22,680
I know it's not a bad thing,

386
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:26,140
but I still feel
a bit uncomfortable inside.

387
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,000
I think anyone would

388
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,640
feel uncomfortable in this situation.

389
00:23:32,830 --> 00:23:35,760
After all, it's a project
you've built from scratch.

390
00:23:35,830 --> 00:23:36,680
However,

391
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:38,070
it doesn't necessarily mean the professor

392
00:23:38,070 --> 00:23:40,510
and the school
don't recognize your abilities.

393
00:23:40,510 --> 00:23:41,310
I think

394
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,160
they probably want you
to focus your energy

395
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,760
on more important research,

396
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:46,920
right?

397
00:23:47,790 --> 00:23:50,390
He said there would be
new arrangements for me.

398
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,200
But this project is something

399
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,060
we've been in charge of all along.

400
00:23:55,590 --> 00:23:57,520
I was suddenly told to hand it over.

401
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:01,160
It feels like I'm detached from something
I was a part of.

402
00:24:01,160 --> 00:24:02,310
I feel empty inside.

403
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:05,440
Well,

404
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:09,270
let me make an analogy
that may not be entirely accurate.

405
00:24:09,270 --> 00:24:11,270
This project is like a big tree.

406
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:13,550
You helped it take root

407
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:16,420
and built its foundation layer by layer.

408
00:24:17,070 --> 00:24:17,750
Therefore,

409
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,610
no matter how tall and big

410
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:21,340
its branches and leaves grow,

411
00:24:21,590 --> 00:24:22,990
as long as it's this tree,

412
00:24:23,310 --> 00:24:25,040
its roots will always be yours.

413
00:24:27,790 --> 00:24:29,400
So you mean,

414
00:24:29,590 --> 00:24:30,680
the roots are mine,

415
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,980
but the tree belongs to someone else?

416
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,270
Even if this tree

417
00:24:35,270 --> 00:24:37,310
ends up bearing someone else's name,

418
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:38,000
Lin Zhixia,

419
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:39,880
as long as you want to,

420
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:41,440
you can even plant a whole forest

421
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,640
easily in the future.

422
00:24:43,270 --> 00:24:44,730
Given your capabilities,

423
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:47,620
there's no need
to hold onto one single tree.

424
00:24:51,680 --> 00:24:54,610
Jiang Yubai, why do you have
so much confidence in me?

425
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:57,690
It's not about confidence.

426
00:24:58,270 --> 00:24:59,330
It's because I know

427
00:25:00,050 --> 00:25:02,580
you're the most amazing person
I've ever met.

428
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:07,490
You have more faith in me
than I have in myself.

429
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:11,400
Alright, time to sleep.

430
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:14,920
I need to go to school
to hand it over tomorrow morning.

431
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:17,340
Good night.

432
00:25:18,550 --> 00:25:19,210
Good night.

433
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:38,810
Jiang Yubai, I'm missing you so much.

434
00:25:40,290 --> 00:25:43,300
[Lin Zhixia]

435
00:25:43,340 --> 00:25:45,290
[Jiang Yubai]

436
00:25:44,550 --> 00:25:45,910
I'm coming to see you now.

437
00:25:45,910 --> 00:25:49,640
[I'm coming to see you now.]

438
00:25:49,670 --> 00:25:52,710
[Jiang Yubai]

439
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,680
It's too late. Let's meet this weekend.

440
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:53,440
I'll go meet you.

441
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:57,200
[Lin Zhixia]

442
00:25:54,570 --> 00:25:57,400
Okay, I actually have something
to tell you, too.

443
00:25:57,350 --> 00:25:58,700
[What is it?]

444
00:25:58,770 --> 00:26:02,000
[Lin Zhixia]

445
00:25:59,550 --> 00:26:00,510
What is it?

446
00:26:02,570 --> 00:26:04,010
You'll know soon.

447
00:26:04,510 --> 00:26:06,270
Go to sleep now. Good night.

448
00:26:05,590 --> 00:26:07,750
[Something good. You'll know soon.]

449
00:26:07,790 --> 00:26:08,940
[Go to sleep now. Good night.]

450
00:26:13,830 --> 00:26:14,590
Good night.

451
00:26:54,020 --> 00:26:58,000
[Fun Biking]

452
00:27:04,090 --> 00:27:07,210
[Fun Biking]

453
00:27:08,590 --> 00:27:10,070
Duan, come on in.

454
00:27:10,530 --> 00:27:18,390
[Fun Biking]

455
00:27:10,750 --> 00:27:11,410
Have a seat.

456
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,030
Long time no see.

457
00:27:20,580 --> 00:27:25,140
[Fun Biking]

458
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:22,070
Duan,

459
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:22,960
look,

460
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,460
we haven't seen you at the office lately,

461
00:27:25,510 --> 00:27:27,840
and everyone's lost their energy at work!

462
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:29,070
The company

463
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:31,040
really can't do without you.

464
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:33,400
Just tell me

465
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:35,400
what you want from me.

466
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,680
Let's cut to the chase instead of

467
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:39,080
beating around the bush.

468
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,750
Why isn't Mr. Duan
making a fuss this time?

469
00:27:42,750 --> 00:27:44,790
I thought he'd definitely
chew us out a bit.

470
00:27:44,790 --> 00:27:46,050
He's so nice this time.

471
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:48,960
Here's the thing.

472
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:50,400
Remember

473
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:54,200
the top tech expert you talked to before?

474
00:27:54,750 --> 00:27:57,080
I mean Dr. Zhou,
who came back from abroad.

475
00:27:57,780 --> 00:27:58,750
He is now

476
00:27:59,920 --> 00:28:01,590
very popular in the market.

477
00:28:02,070 --> 00:28:03,830
An investor has even made it clear

478
00:28:03,830 --> 00:28:05,270
that he will immediately invest in

479
00:28:05,270 --> 00:28:07,000
whichever company he chooses.

480
00:28:09,310 --> 00:28:10,030
So

481
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,790
you want to hire Dr. Zhou now?

482
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:15,070
Duan,

483
00:28:16,790 --> 00:28:18,200
I've always believed you were right.

484
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:19,590
You're really farsighted.

485
00:28:19,590 --> 00:28:21,000
We all just...

486
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:21,550
Okay.

487
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:25,370
It's a deal then.

488
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:27,200
I'll find a chance to talk to him.

489
00:28:27,200 --> 00:28:28,660
You're doing a good thing.

490
00:28:29,590 --> 00:28:30,200
Yes.

491
00:28:30,270 --> 00:28:31,000
However...

492
00:28:33,550 --> 00:28:35,240
Could you not make the meeting

493
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:36,680
so tense?

494
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:37,550
What?

495
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:40,000
Are meetings this tense now without me?

496
00:28:40,030 --> 00:28:41,680
We need to be more lively, right?

497
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:42,480
Yes, exactly.

498
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:43,680
Why so tense?

499
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:44,380
Yeah.

500
00:28:44,590 --> 00:28:46,590
I'll have someone
buy some snacks and drinks.

501
00:28:46,590 --> 00:28:48,240
Let's eat and talk. How about that?

502
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:49,030
Nice.

503
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:50,440
Good. What are we going to discuss?

504
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:52,100
Everyone, get ready. Come on.

505
00:28:57,030 --> 00:28:58,200
Mr. Duan,

506
00:28:58,310 --> 00:29:01,160
what a rare occasion for you
to treat me to a meal for celebration.

507
00:29:01,160 --> 00:29:03,510
Do I need a reason to celebrate with you?

508
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:05,550
Come on, cheers.

509
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:11,000
You really helped me a lot
with getting this issue solved

510
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,510
for my company this time.

511
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:15,270
Besides, can't I just treat you to a meal?

512
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:16,720
Yes, sure.

513
00:29:20,270 --> 00:29:22,670
You've grown up
and learned to be grateful.

514
00:29:26,920 --> 00:29:28,920
Why are you staring at me? Eat up now.

515
00:29:30,400 --> 00:29:30,960
Okay.

516
00:29:34,070 --> 00:29:34,800
Nice meat...

517
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:40,850
Anything wrong?

518
00:29:42,990 --> 00:29:45,270
Tell me what you're cooking up again.

519
00:29:45,270 --> 00:29:47,530
Out with it
while I'm in a good mood today.

520
00:29:56,680 --> 00:29:57,830
I do have something

521
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:01,050
that I want to get your take on.

522
00:30:07,550 --> 00:30:08,510
Well...

523
00:30:10,830 --> 00:30:12,440
A friend of mine

524
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:14,790
has a beloved one

525
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:16,820
and wants to confess his feelings to her.

526
00:30:16,820 --> 00:30:19,680
But they are childhood friends.

527
00:30:22,270 --> 00:30:23,920
So he doesn't know what to do.

528
00:30:28,940 --> 00:30:30,920
What's so hard about it?

529
00:30:31,070 --> 00:30:32,320
Just tell her directly.

530
00:30:32,320 --> 00:30:34,160
Calm down. Let me finish first.

531
00:30:36,790 --> 00:30:38,920
My friend is mainly afraid that

532
00:30:40,510 --> 00:30:42,170
if he confesses his love to her

533
00:30:42,510 --> 00:30:43,570
and gets rejected,

534
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:44,590
or if

535
00:30:44,750 --> 00:30:45,960
they get together

536
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:47,400
but break up later,

537
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,920
they wouldn't even be friends anymore.

538
00:30:50,310 --> 00:30:51,310
This girl holds

539
00:30:52,510 --> 00:30:54,370
a very special place in his heart.

540
00:30:55,510 --> 00:30:56,200
So,

541
00:30:57,310 --> 00:30:58,310
what should he do?

542
00:31:01,590 --> 00:31:02,850
Which friend of yours?

543
00:31:03,960 --> 00:31:05,000
You don't know him.

544
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,400
Never mind which friend.

545
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:07,550
Just tell me

546
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:09,160
your take on this.

547
00:31:10,310 --> 00:31:11,720
Which friend of yours don't I know?

548
00:31:11,720 --> 00:31:12,960
Just tell me who it is.

549
00:31:13,310 --> 00:31:15,750
Well... Forget about who it is for now.

550
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:17,650
Just answer my question first.

551
00:31:17,680 --> 00:31:20,830
From a girl's perspective,

552
00:31:21,270 --> 00:31:23,680
do you think this girl would agree
to be together with him?

553
00:31:23,680 --> 00:31:24,440
Or rather,

554
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:27,510
if your childhood friend
confesses his love to you,

555
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:28,510
would you agree to be with him?

556
00:31:28,510 --> 00:31:29,160
No.

557
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:33,400
Who would date their childhood friends?
That's ridiculous.

558
00:31:38,310 --> 00:31:39,510
She is

559
00:31:39,510 --> 00:31:40,680
not you.

560
00:31:40,790 --> 00:31:42,000
Maybe she thinks

561
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:44,070
that growing up together

562
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,440
and knowing each other well

563
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,790
would make
for a good romantic relationship.

564
00:31:47,790 --> 00:31:48,510
Right?

565
